From 18ab53f49787341f75e24339f1bdcda988ee5df4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:18:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Host-side SET VOLUME/LABEL and SHOW VOLUME (#13)

Copies of a blank VMS-initialized volume all carry the blank's label,
and two volumes with one label can't both be mounted /SYSTEM on a node
(they clash on DISK$label), so each copy needed a trip through VMS for
SET VOLUME/LABEL.

    ./ods2 kits.dsk SET VOLUME/LABEL=ITANKITS
    ./ods2 kits.dsk SHOW VOLUME

ods2_set_volume_label() rewrites every copy of the home block: the
home block and its cluster fillers (INDEXF.SYS VBNs 2 to 2v) and the
backup home block's cluster (VBNs 2v+1 to 3v), per spec 5.1.3-5.1.4.
On the real starter volume that is 8 blocks, LBN 1-5 and 1032-1034.
The copies aren't identical - each names its own position in HOMELBN
and HOMEVBN - so each is changed in place, HM2$T_VOLNAME set, checksum1
then checksum2 recomputed.

Nothing is written unless every one of those blocks is first found to
be a valid home block naming its own position and otherwise identical
to the primary, with the primary and backup among them. A volume set
member (structure name, RVN or set count) is refused. The primary is
written last, so an interruption leaves VMS seeing the old label
consistently, and every copy is read back. Labels are 1-12 of letters,
digits, $, _ and -, uppercased.

SHOW VOLUME reports the label, owner, format, structure level, cluster
size, maximum files, owner UIC, volume set, and total (SCB$L_VOLSIZE)
and free blocks (ods2_volume_space(), counting BITMAP.SYS).

cli_volume_label_check.sh runs on the real starter volume: all 8
copies relabelled with their own LBN/VBN and valid checksums and no
other block changed (checked across the whole image), the relabelled
volume still takes files, and with the image left byte for byte
unchanged: bad labels, a damaged backup copy (named in the message), a
volume set member, and a volume missing its backup cluster.

Not yet checked on VMS: MOUNT and ANALYZE/DISK of a relabelled volume.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WA1cTxSh5f8UrT87d9WhcQ
